# SV-COMP ARG-V-C Benchmarks

Benchmarks generated from real-world C OSS code found on github.

Contact: [Nathanael Steven](nathanaelsteven@u.boisestate.edu) (main developer)
[Dr. Elena Sherman](elenasherman@boisestate.edu)

Where full verification is intractable, separate `_tract` source and task files apply restricted bounds or concrete input values.

---

## superfasthash (DrKLO/Telegram)

[Source](https://github.com/DrKLO/Telegram/blob/009e97356f966bb81eceba113d210230bf383122/TMessagesProj/jni/voip/webrtc/base/third_party/superfasthash/superfasthash.c)

Hash algorithm operating on byte arrays with bitwise operations. A bound controls the number of input bytes. The tractable variant (`_tract`) reduces the bound to 8 (at most 1 main-loop iteration), making valid-memsafety and termination provable.

| Task file | Properties |
|---|---|
| `DrKLO_Telegram_superfasthash.yml` | no-overflow=**false** |
| `DrKLO_Telegram_superfasthash_unreach.yml` | unreach-call=**false** |
| `DrKLO_Telegram_superfasthash_tract.yml` | valid-memsafety=true, termination=true |

---

## endianconv (antirez/redis)

[Source](https://github.com/antirez/redis/blob/e8726d18e5bab24cbfcb0a0c36f21ce5a1140471/src/endianconv.c)

Byte-order reversal for 16/32/64-bit integers using bitwise ops and byte swaps. Assertions verify the double-reversal identity.

| Task file | Properties |
|---|---|
| `antirez_redis_endianconv.yml` | unreach-call=true, valid-memsafety=true, termination=true |

---

## fastjson (antirez/redis)

[Source](https://github.com/antirez/redis/blob/e8726d18e5bab24cbfcb0a0c36f21ce5a1140471/modules/vector-sets/fastjson.c)

Lightweight JSON field extractor using mutually recursive token parsers. The tractable variant pins input to a single field with a symbolic string value.

| Task file | Properties |
|---|---|
| `antirez_redis_fastjson.yml` | no-overflow=true, valid-memsafety=true, termination=true |
| `antirez_redis_fastjson_tract.yml` | unreach-call=true, no-overflow=true, termination=true |

Note: unreach-call is only in the `_tract` variant because the base file's mutual recursion makes it intractable for both tools.

---

## localtime (antirez/redis)

[Source](https://github.com/antirez/redis/blob/e8726d18e5bab24cbfcb0a0c36f21ce5a1140471/src/localtime.c)

Lock-free `localtime()` implementation. Assertions verify computed `tm_hour`, `tm_min`, `tm_sec`, `tm_wday` are within valid calendar ranges. The `_unsafe` variant widens input to expose the Y2038 signed overflow bug. Each expected-false property is isolated to its own task file.

| Task file | Properties |
|---|---|
| `antirez_redis_localtime.yml` | unreach-call=true, no-overflow=true, termination=true |
| `antirez_redis_localtime_tract.yml` | unreach-call=true, no-overflow=true, termination=true |
| `antirez_redis_localtime_unsafe.yml` | no-overflow=**false** |
| `antirez_redis_localtime_unsafe_unreach.yml` | unreach-call=**false** |
| `antirez_redis_localtime_unsafe_term.yml` | termination=true |
| `antirez_redis_localtime_unsafe_tract.yml` | no-overflow=**false** |
| `antirez_redis_localtime_unsafe_tract_unreach.yml` | unreach-call=**false** |

Note: `localtime_unsafe*` files declare `data_model: ILP32`. The Y2038 overflow is a 32-bit `long` width issue; the ILP32 model is intentional.

---

## mt19937-64 (antirez/redis)

[Source](https://github.com/antirez/redis/blob/e8726d18e5bab24cbfcb0a0c36f21ce5a1140471/src/mt19937-64.c)

Mersenne Twister 64-bit PRNG. The scalar-seeded variant (`mt19937-64`) and array-seeded variant (`mt19937-64_array`) cover no-overflow, valid-memsafety, and termination. The unreach-call property requires concrete seeds, handled via separate `_unreach_*` task files for each output type (`ll`, `ull`, `r1`–`r3`). The array variant has a tractable valid-memsafety variant.

| Task file | Properties |
|---|---|
| `antirez_redis_mt19937-64.yml` | valid-memsafety=true, no-overflow=true, termination=true |
| `antirez_redis_mt19937-64_array.yml` | valid-memsafety=true, no-overflow=true, termination=true |
| `antirez_redis_mt19937-64_array_valid-memsafety_tract.yml` | valid-memsafety=true |
| `antirez_redis_mt19937-64_unreach_ll.yml` | unreach-call=true |
| `antirez_redis_mt19937-64_unreach_ull.yml` | unreach-call=true |
| `antirez_redis_mt19937-64_unreach_r1.yml` | unreach-call=true |
| `antirez_redis_mt19937-64_unreach_r2.yml` | unreach-call=true |
| `antirez_redis_mt19937-64_unreach_r3.yml` | unreach-call=true |

---

## strl (antirez/redis)

[Source](https://github.com/antirez/redis/blob/e8726d18e5bab24cbfcb0a0c36f21ce5a1140471/src/strl.c)

`strlcpy` and `strlcat`: bounded string copy and concatenation. Assertions verify return-value semantics and null-termination. The tractable variant uses smaller fixed-size buffers.

| Task file | Properties |
|---|---|
| `antirez_redis_strl.yml` | unreach-call=true, valid-memsafety=true, termination=true |
| `antirez_redis_strl_tract.yml` | unreach-call=true, termination=true |

