## sorts (natsteven)



Classic sorting algorithms split into individual benchmark files: bubble (`_bub`), insertion (`_ins`), selection (`_sel`), merge (`_mer`), and an unsorted baseline (`_unsort`). Bubble sort uses `xor_swap`; selection and unsort use the standard `swap` helper. The merge sort uses stack-allocated VLAs. Tractable variants reduce array size or pin inputs for unreach-call and termination coverage.

| Task file | Properties |
|---|---|
| `natsteven_sorts_bub.yml` | unreach-call=true, valid-memsafety=true, termination=true |
| `natsteven_sorts_bub_tract.yml` | unreach-call=true |
| `natsteven_sorts_bub_swap_tract.yml` | unreach-call=true |
| `natsteven_sorts_ins.yml` | unreach-call=true, valid-memsafety=true, termination=true |
| `natsteven_sorts_ins_tract.yml` | unreach-call=true |
| `natsteven_sorts_mer.yml` | unreach-call=true, valid-memsafety=true, termination=true |
| `natsteven_sorts_mer_tract.yml` | unreach-call=true |
| `natsteven_sorts_mer_tract_term.yml` | termination=true |
| `natsteven_sorts_sel.yml` | unreach-call=true, valid-memsafety=true, termination=true |
| `natsteven_sorts_sel_tract.yml` | unreach-call=true, termination=true |
| `natsteven_sorts_unsort.yml` | unreach-call=**false**, valid-memsafety=true |
| `natsteven_sorts_unsort_term.yml` | termination=true |

Note: `_bub`, `_ins`, `_sel` base files time out for unreach-call; their `_tract` variants provide coverage. `_bub_tract` uses `xor_swap`; `_bub_swap_tract` is an identical SIZE=4 variant using the standard `swap` helper to compare tractability across swap implementations. `_mer` base times out for unreach-call and termination; `_mer_tract` (both inputs pinned, unreach-call only) and `_mer_tract_term` (full nondet, termination only) cover both properties. `_unsort` unreach-call is expected false (shuffle may produce a sorted permutation); termination is split into `_unsort_term`.

